---
title: Archive
layout: layouts/pagealign.liquid
permalink: /archive/
eleventyImport:
  collections: ["post"]
---
{%- comment %} Every post, newest first. The homepage shows only the most
   recent few and links here — the source's own "…see full archives" pattern
   (index.liquid), which needs somewhere to point. {% endcomment -%}
<ol class="posts h-feed">
{%- assign allPosts = collections.post | reverse -%}
{%- for post in allPosts %}
  {%- comment %} The social counts, and the post-type icon, are captured HERE,
     before the `page: post` override below, on purpose. @11ty/font-awesome
     registers each icon's sprite symbol against `this.page.url` (plugin.js:51).
     Rendered inside the override, every {{ "{% icon %}" }} filed its symbol under the
     POST's url while the listing page emitted a <use href="#..."> for a symbol
     that was never in its own bundle — the icon painted nothing. Capturing
     outside the override files the symbol against this listing page, where
     {{ "{% getBundle %}" }} outputs it. The override itself stays: date filters must
     read each post's own front matter (see post-list-entry.liquid). {% endcomment -%}
  {%- capture socialHtml %}{% include "partials/post-social-counts.liquid", post: post %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- capture postTypeIconHtml %}{% include "partials/post-type-icon.liquid", post: post %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- include "partials/post-list-entry.liquid", post: post, page: post, socialHtml: socialHtml, postTypeIconHtml: postTypeIconHtml -%}
{%- endfor %}
</ol>
